  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Which of the following is congruent to $0$ modulo $4?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, recall that \n\n$$\na≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a=kn,\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in Z.$ In other words, when $a$ is divided by $n,$ there is no remainder. This means that any integer multiple of $4$ is congruent to $0$ modulo $4.$\n\nTherefore, since $4\\,|\\,52,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n52≡13\\cdot 4≡13\\cdot 0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4).\n$$\n\nNone of the other options are multiples of $4.$",
